            {
                "entry_id": "f7cb91e9-7fa8-31c1-9734-d3d563c7c293",
                "word": "lisseur",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2cbefa5a-6d3c-40c1-944c-3122ddbaa659",
                        "entry_id": "f7cb91e9-7fa8-31c1-9734-d3d563c7c293",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lisseurs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                        "entry_id": "f7cb91e9-7fa8-31c1-9734-d3d563c7c293",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère de ce qui est lisse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37cabffd-845c-47e3-a3be-d4051936defd",
                                "sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                                "text": "[…] des pierres incertaines et la lisseur perfide des neiges, que de surprises, que de douleurs […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6ccf8c9-2309-4792-92a1-d7d71f8a9004",
                                "sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                                "text": "[…] c’était l’enveloppe des corps, une couleur, une rondeur, une lisseur dont on pouvait tirer des photos, des sculptures, des toiles […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aa940f9-1d84-4483-9f53-b8d1642feccb",
                                "sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                                "text": "C’est son teint anémone irisée de paillettes nacrées qui scintillent sur la lisseur de sa peau."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a3c2899-cccc-42b6-adaf-35389fcd10e0",
                                "sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                                "text": "Lui, quand le chat s’était enfui, avait senti des vertèbres dures glisser sous la lisseur du poil […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eec57a72-dee6-4f12-88be-4a4e9fc7011c",
                                "sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                                "text": "Pablo Casals ne voulut jamais renoncer aux cordes de boyau, ce qui donnait à son jeu un ton râpeux et fruste qu’on peut certes préférer à la trop parfaite lisseur des nouveaux instruments à cordes métalliques."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ec81e4a8-6dca-48c2-bb24-d69f53e90b26",
                        "source_entry_id": "f7cb91e9-7fa8-31c1-9734-d3d563c7c293",
                        "source_sense_id": "9049bb34-06d9-3935-b8e4-f0e52a2674f5",
                        "target_lang_word": "smoothness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "smoothness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3985c8ba-89cd-3ded-a04f-8289d782a262",
                                        "entry_id": "7ababfe9-d9a2-3e43-9d26-ee640fdb52ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being smooth; the degree or measure of said condition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91ff45c0-c16c-4f02-880b-663497d84d43",
                                                "sense_id": "3985c8ba-89cd-3ded-a04f-8289d782a262",
                                                "text": "The admirable smoothness of the riding also reflected the greatest credit on those who, despite the difficulties caused by the shortage of men and materials, have succeeded in maintaining the track in such first-class order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b2b8a2b-1620-4712-8ad1-e38af10f8f4b",
                                                "sense_id": "3985c8ba-89cd-3ded-a04f-8289d782a262",
                                                "text": "The ‘smoothness’ of distributions can be understood in various senses, this is why we used quotation marks before; further we will drop them. The smoothness can be understood as the differentiability of the distribution function, boundedness of some of its derivatives, the existence of the absolutely continuous component, the decrease of the characteristic function with a certain rate, the validity of the Cramér condition, the condition #92;sigma(#92;Phi)#92;rightarrow 0 as n#92;rightarrow#92;infty, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42c5ec1d-b6b3-48d3-bd7f-20e08d8ce0ee",
                                                "sense_id": "3985c8ba-89cd-3ded-a04f-8289d782a262",
                                                "text": "With it,^([a pavement profile]) paving operations can be adjusted \"on the fly\" to maintain or improve smoothness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c68959f-e6bf-31b1-8fb6-8e5af2ec799e",
                                        "entry_id": "7ababfe9-d9a2-3e43-9d26-ee640fdb52ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The highest order of derivative (the differentiability class) over a given domain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b301ef2d-0bc8-41d9-99d4-cfb7af77fd6b",
                                                "sense_id": "1c68959f-e6bf-31b1-8fb6-8e5af2ec799e",
                                                "text": "Smoothness can vary from 0 (for a nondifferentiable function) to infinity (for a smooth function)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c48f9145-2648-34e3-8a9b-e7f0c7d7c13c",
                                        "entry_id": "7ababfe9-d9a2-3e43-9d26-ee640fdb52ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quantity measured by the modulus of smoothness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c327df3d-e915-4d94-90b5-b72203ab8306",
                                                "sense_id": "c48f9145-2648-34e3-8a9b-e7f0c7d7c13c",
                                                "text": "A central problem in approximation theory is to characterize the best approximation of a function by polynomials, or other classes of simple functions, in terms of the smoothness of the function. In this chapter, we study the characterization of the best approximation by polynomials on the sphere. In the classical setting of one variable, the smoothness of a function on #92;mathbbS¹ is described by the modulus of smoothness, defined by the forward difference."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
